# File: scripts/__tests__/test-selection-gate.test.mjs, scripts/__tests__/nmg-sdlc-smoke.test.mjs, scripts/__tests__/repository-surfaces.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/643-rerun-only-what-a-gate-has-not-proven-reuse-passed-results-scope-surfaces-on-fallback-paths-and-carry-smoke-records-forward/requirements.md
Feature: Rerun only what a gate has not proven: reuse passed results, scope surfaces on fallback paths, and carry smoke records forward

  @SCN001
  Scenario: A gate rerun at an unchanged tree runs only what did not pass
    Given a pre-merge gate in which the test command and one provider passed and another provider failed
    When the gate runs again at the same head with a new run id
    Then only the failed provider runs
    And the passed results are recorded with the new request and "reused" naming the first run

  @SCN002
  Scenario Outline: Nothing is reused when <condition>
    Given a pre-merge gate that passed
    And <condition>
    When the gate runs again
    Then every applicable validation runs and no result is "reused"

    Examples:
      | condition                    |
      | the head moved               |
      | the working tree changed     |
      | the spec changed             |
      | reuse is turned off          |
      | "--fresh true" is passed     |

  @SCN002
  Scenario: The selected tests always run
    Given a "selected" gate run that passed
    When the gate runs again at the same head
    Then the selected tests and their coverage check run again
    And the other passed results are reused

  @SCN002
  Scenario: A result that did not pass is never reused
    Given a gate run whose test command failed, or whose artifact cannot be read
    When the gate runs again
    Then the test command runs

  @SCN003
  Scenario: A fallback path runs every test and only the surfaces the change affects
    Given a project whose "site" surface binds a validation and whose "package.json" is a fallback path
    And a branch that changes "package.json" and "site/index.html"
    When the gate runs and the selection call names the surface "other"
    Then the selection is "all" with reason "fallback_path" and every test runs
    And the surfaces are "site" and "other"

  @SCN003
  Scenario: A fallback change that touches no surface selects none
    Given a branch that changes only "package.json"
    When the gate runs and the selection call names no surface
    Then every test runs and the surface-bound validation passes as "surface_not_selected"

  @SCN004
  Scenario: A project with no surface-bound validation is not asked
    Given a project in which no surface names a validation
    And a branch that changes the fallback path "package.json"
    When the gate runs
    Then Claude is not asked and every declared surface is selected

  @SCN005
  Scenario: A smoke surface record is carried forward over inert changes
    Given a surface record made at an earlier head
    And only tests, specs, documentation and the version changed since
    When the smoke gate checks the surface
    Then the record proves it and the evidence names both heads

  @SCN005
  Scenario Outline: A smoke surface record goes stale when <change>
    Given a surface record made at an earlier head
    And <change>
    When the smoke gate checks the surface
    Then the gate fails with "nmg-sdlc-smoke surface not exercised"

    Examples:
      | change                                          |
      | a workflow file changed                         |
      | a source file changed                           |
      | the hooks module changed                        |
      | a version mirror changed another line           |
      | a test moved out of the test directory          |
      | the record head is not an ancestor of the head  |
      | git cannot list the changed paths               |

  @SCN006
  Scenario: The hooks module and the smoke provider require every surface they serve
    Given this repository's steering manifest
    When "hooks/register.ts", "hooks/hooks.json" or the smoke provider changes
    Then every smoke surface the file serves is required
    And smoke steering says which earlier surface records still count

  @SCN007
  Scenario: The controller tests run in parallel and CI runs no empty job
    Given the contract suite and the CI workflow
    When the suite runs
    Then the controller tests are spread over four files sharing one fixture module
    And CI has no job that selects tests by a name no test has
